From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: The Playport authors <dev@playport.dev>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 23:43:43 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] wsi/metal: on iOS a swap chain the layer scales is not
 suboptimal

vkQueuePresentKHR returned VK_SUBOPTIMAL_KHR whenever the layer's
bounds, in pixels, differed from the swap chain's extent. On iOS the
layer is the embedding app's, and it scales the drawable to its bounds
(drawableSize is the extent), so another size still shows whole. Wine's
surface reports the window's client size as the current extent, so a
game whose window is smaller than the screen got a swap chain of that
size, a suboptimal result on every present and a recreation after each:
The Witcher 3 under DXVK presented two frames and stopped. Do not
report suboptimal for the size on iOS.

Class: ios-port
Evidence: docs/evidence/2026-09-26-vulkan-d3d11-d3d12.md
Offered-upstream: no
---
 src/vulkan/wsi/wsi_common_metal.c | 11 +++++++++++
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/vulkan/wsi/wsi_common_metal.c b/src/vulkan/wsi/wsi_common_metal.c
index 08f4cee..50bac21 100644
--- a/src/vulkan/wsi/wsi_common_metal.c
+++ b/src/vulkan/wsi/wsi_common_metal.c
@@ -741,7 +741,18 @@ wsi_metal_swapchain_queue_present(struct wsi_swapchain *wsi_chain,
 
    uint32_t width = 0u, height = 0u;
    wsi_metal_layer_size(chain->surface->pLayer, &width, &height);
+#if TARGET_OS_IPHONE
+   /* On iOS the layer belongs to the app that embeds the driver, and it
+    * scales the drawable (drawableSize is the swap chain's extent) to its
+    * bounds, as CAMetalLayer's contentsGravity says. A swap chain of another
+    * size is presented whole, so it is not suboptimal. Reporting it so made
+    * a caller whose window is smaller than the screen (Wine's surface
+    * reports the window's client size) recreate its swap chain after every
+    * present: The Witcher 3 under DXVK presented two frames and stopped. */
+   bool is_optimal = true;
+#else
    bool is_optimal = (width == chain->extent.width && height == chain->extent.height);
+#endif
    kk_wsi_trace(1, "present image=%u id=%llu wait=%d layer=%ux%u chain=%ux%u\n", image_index,
                 (unsigned long long)present_id, present_id && wsi_chain->present_wait_enabled,
                 width, height, chain->extent.width, chain->extent.height);
